FINDINGS:
1. [MAJOR] src/parser.rs:1813 — `kind_starts_operand` omits `TokenKind::This` while `parse_primary` handles `This` as `Variable("this")` (src/parser.rs:2575), so `xs at this` and `length of this` never trigger `at_index_ahead` and misparse as separate statements (analyzer `Unknown variable 'at'` instead of the runtime index error) — it matters because `this` is bound inside object methods and is user-reachable as an operand, and both engines agree on the wrong answer (bootstrap/compiler.rb:1146 omits `this` while bootstrap/compiler.rb:2177 handles it) so byte-identity/differential tests cannot catch it — concrete fix: add `TokenKind::This`/`"this"` to both operand tables (`kind_starts_operand` and `is_operand_start`), with a test for `xs at this` and `length of this` against the bracket/call spellings.
REVIEW VERDICT: FINDINGS 1
